## Devices

`emulator:` (or `--emulator`) names the AVD: it is used if running, booted otherwise.
With no `emulator:`, the order is: the one running emulator, else the one emulator still
booting (waited on), else the only existing AVD (booted); otherwise the command fails and
lists the AVDs. `--device <serial>` targets any attached device, including
a physical one; it is used as is and never booted (`run` says `Using emulator: <name> (<serial>)`),
and a serial that is not attached is an error naming the attached devices. On a physical device the demo-mode and animation settings are skipped
unless `--allow-device-settings` is given. `--headless` boots without a window, and so do
`GRANTIVA_EMULATOR_HEADLESS=1` (or `true`/`yes`) and `CI` set to any value other than empty,
`0` or `false` (as CI services set it). Nothing else makes a boot windowless: without one of
them an emulator Grantiva boots gets a window, even when stdout is not a terminal
(`serial=$(grantiva emulator ensure ...)`, a pipe, an agent).

`grantiva build build` only compiles: it never resolves or boots a device, so `emulator:` does
not apply to it, and its help does not list `--emulator`, `--headless` or
`--allow-device-settings` (they are still accepted, hidden, and change nothing). Where the variant has ABI split APKs, the one reported is for `--device`'s
ABI when given, else for this host's emulators (`arm64-v8a` on Apple silicon). A `--device`
serial must already be attached; otherwise the command fails naming the attached devices.
`grantiva build install` resolves the device as above and logs `Booting AVD <name> as
<serial>` when it has to boot one.

The application ID a run installs and tests is the app's own: the Gradle output metadata's
`applicationId` for a built variant, or the APK's (read with `apkanalyzer`) for `--app-file`.
`application_id` in the config is used only when there is no app to read it from
(`--no-build`); when it disagrees with the app, the app wins and a warning names both.
`--application-id` overrides the test target, with a warning when it disagrees with the app;
the APK is still installed under its own ID.

`--no-build` skips the Gradle build and assumes the app is already installed: nothing is
installed, and `build install --no-build` says `(install skipped)` in its `Done` line. With
`--app-file <apk>` as well, that APK is installed and only the build is skipped (`build
install`, `run`, `diff capture` alike).

Flags: `--module`, `--variant`, `--application-id`, `--emulator`, `--device`,
`--allow-device-settings`, `--headless`, `--logs-tag`. iOS flags such as `--scheme` are
rejected on Android, and vice versa. `GRANTIVA_PLATFORM=android` or `--platform android`
forces the platform when both config files exist.

